{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 14219 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f1be9a66ae883989de403c984f053d8b015fba2cae194fa4bc636e05d2d9c53b" :edb/db-before-t 14218 :edb/db-after-t 14219 :edb/tx-data [[13194139547531 50 #inst "2026-11-11T22:09:33.774Z" 13194139547531 17592186576411 true] [17592186735164 1071 "The nonparallel vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ start at $O$, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![](images/ce/cee2a501a390c40bc1100336ff4a7cda3e7a070dff7dc0470b1762833a7a677a.png)\n\nThe path $O\\to P\\to C$ is already drawn. It has $\\overrightarrow{OP}=2\\mathbf{b}$ and $PC=|\\mathbf{a}|$.\n\nCompare the direction of $\\overrightarrow{PC}$ with $\\mathbf{a}$. If $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$, what is $\\lambda$?" 13194139547531 17592186576411 false] [17592186735164 1071 "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/af/afdd59dbd0050ed655b319b015b2ef03de3c8a314b8ba5e9c29c5755be0a4b66.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$." 13194139547531 17592186576411 true] [17592186735164 1074 "Draw $2\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$, then complete the path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ of $\\mathbf{c}$.\n\n![](images/ce/cee2a501a390c40bc1100336ff4a7cda3e7a070dff7dc0470b1762833a7a677a.png)\n\nThe vector $\\overrightarrow{PC}$ points left, while $\\mathbf{a}$ points right. Their lengths are equal, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the two path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, their coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records direction; the equal lengths give magnitude $1$." 13194139547531 17592186576411 true] [17592186735164 1074 "The vector $\\overrightarrow{PC}$ points left, while $\\mathbf{a}$ points right. Their lengths are equal, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nFollowing the drawn path gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, their coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records direction; the equal lengths give magnitude $1$." 13194139547531 17592186576411 false]] :edb/tempids {}}
